# CP19.1 — two sentences.

README.md
tests/test_charts.py
checkpoints/cp19_1.allowlist

# tests/test_charts.py was added to this allowlist mid-checkpoint, asked and
# approved. See the block below.

# --- F45. The slogan, replaced by the composition -----------------------------
#
# §1 told a reader that 33,995 dispatches and 36 contacts were the same system
# and never said what the other 33,959 were or what they cost. The sentence
# asserted the distinction the whole result turns on and never showed it.
#
# metrics.json has no breakdown by verb, so retries cannot be separated from
# rail switches and the README now says so rather than guessing a split. What it
# does have is the spend, and the spend closes the composition exactly:
#
#     spend_paise                       170,335
#     (33,995 - 36) x 5 paise    =      169,795     retry / switch_rail
#     36 x 15 paise              =          540     one contact, sms channel
#                                       -------
#                                       170,335     exact
#
# Nothing else fits inside that total: no WhatsApp at 35 paise, no voice call at
# 400, no escalation at 5,000, and no `do_nothing` at 0 padding the dispatch
# count — a single do_nothing in the total would leave the arithmetic short.
# Costs from PRIORS.md action_cost.*.
#
# 33,959 and 169,795 and 540 are NOT in the README. They are subtractions and
# products of artefact values, and no artefact holds them, so CHT-3 would reject
# them. The two ways round that are the two this project refuses: a fenced code
# block, which CHT-3 strips before extracting numbers and which would pass while
# checking nothing, and spelling the digits out as words. The prose gives the
# backed numbers and leaves the arithmetic to the reader. The derivation lives
# here instead, where nothing claims it was checked by a test.

# --- The stop, and what was approved ------------------------------------------
#
# F45 said replace the slogan. The slogan was pinned in two places outside the
# allowlist:
#
#   tests/test_charts.py:350   asserted it verbatim
#   SPEC.md §15.2 (A99)        "The README must say 'far fewer contacts' and
#                              must not permit the reading 'far less work'."
#
# Stopped and asked rather than editing either or quietly keeping the sentence.
# Approved: add tests/test_charts.py, leave SPEC alone. A99 requires the claim,
# not that rendering of it, and the README still makes the claim in the last
# paragraph — "That is why 'far fewer contacts' is not 'less work'." So the
# amendment stands unchanged and the test now pins both halves: the dispatch and
# contact counts against out/metrics.json, and A99's claim as a claim.

# --- F46. The flinch ----------------------------------------------------------
#
# "That is a property of the test account, not a defect in `settle`" deleted
# from §9. The sentence after it — a real decline beside a real capture in one
# verifiable chain is worth more than a clean single capture — is the stronger
# argument and was being made in the same breath as a denial nobody had asked
# for. Nothing else in that paragraph changed.
